#: ../../source/concepts.md:1
msgid "Astrological Concepts"
msgstr "Concepts astrologiques"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:3
msgid "Coordinate System"
msgstr "Système de coordonnées"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:5
msgid "Ecliptic Longitude"
msgstr "Longitude écliptique"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:7
msgid ""
"**Ecliptic longitude** is the position of a celestial body measured along"
" the ecliptic (the Earth's orbital plane around the Sun), expressed in "
"degrees from 0° to 360°."
msgstr ""
"La **longitude écliptique** est la position d'un corps céleste mesurée le"
" long de l'écliptique (plan orbital de la Terre autour du Soleil), "
"exprimée en degrés de 0° à 360°."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:9
msgid "0° = Vernal point (0° Aries)"
msgstr "0° = Point vernal (0° Bélier)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:10
msgid "90° = Summer solstice (0° Cancer)"
msgstr "90° = Solstice d'été (0° Cancer)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:11
msgid "180° = Autumn equinox (0° Libra)"
msgstr "180° = Équinoxe d'automne (0° Balance)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:12
msgid "270° = Winter solstice (0° Capricorn)"
msgstr "270° = Solstice d'hiver (0° Capricorne)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:14
msgid "Ecliptic Latitude"
msgstr "Latitude écliptique"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:16
msgid ""
"**Ecliptic latitude** measures the angular distance of a body above (+) "
"or below (-) the ecliptic plane."
msgstr ""
"La **latitude écliptique** mesure la distance angulaire d'un corps au-"
"dessus (+) ou en-dessous (-) du plan de l'écliptique."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:18
msgid "Distance in AU"
msgstr "Distance en UA"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:20
msgid ""
"The **Astronomical Unit** (AU) is the average Earth-Sun distance, "
"approximately 149.6 million km."
msgstr ""
"L'**Unité Astronomique** (UA) est la distance moyenne Terre-Soleil, "
"environ 149,6 millions de km."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:22
msgid "Astronomical Time"
msgstr "Temps astronomique"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:24
msgid "Coordinated Universal Time (UTC)"
msgstr "Temps Universel Coordonné (UTC)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:26
msgid ""
"**UTC** is the reference time standard, based on international atomic "
"time."
msgstr ""
"Le **UTC** est le standard de temps de référence, basé sur le temps "
"atomique international."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:28
msgid "Julian Day"
msgstr "Jour Julien"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:30
msgid ""
"The **Julian Day** (JD) is a continuous dating system used in astronomy. "
"JD begins at noon UTC on January 1, 4713 BCE in the proleptic Julian "
"calendar."
msgstr ""
"Le **Jour Julien** (JD) est un système de datation continue utilisé en "
"astronomie. Le JD commence à midi UTC le 1er janvier 4713 av. J.-C. du "
"calendrier julien proleptique."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:38
msgid "Celestial Bodies"
msgstr "Corps célestes"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:40
msgid "Ketu calculates the positions of 14 celestial bodies (body IDs 0–13):"
msgstr "Ketu calcule les positions de 14 corps célestes (body IDs 0–13) :"

